  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is amphoteric and strong oxidizing agent and also a component of lead storage batteries.</p><p>In lead storage batteries <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PbO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is used. In this Oxidation state&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pb</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math> so, it is always reduced and behaves as oxidizing agent</p>"
